  "raw_response": "Looking at the examples, I can identify the pattern:\n\n1. **Four corner markers (4s)** define a rectangle region\n2. **Colored blocks** inside the rectangle sit on a grid with a fixed block size\n3. A **small template pattern** outside the rectangle shows how to fill the block grid (each template cell = one block-sized region)\n4. The template is scaled up by the block size and placed starting at the origin of the colored blocks\n\nThe template's existing colors align with the original block positions, and new colors fill gaps between them.\n\n```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    fours = [(r, c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if grid[r][c] == 4]\n    r_min = min(r for r, c in fours)\n    r_max = max(r for r, c in fours)\n    c_min = min(c for r, c in fours)\n    c_max = max(c for r, c in fours)\n    rect_h = r_max - r_min + 1\n    rect_w = c_max - c_min + 1\n    \n    color_cells = {}\n    for r in range(r_min, r_max + 1):\n        for c in range(c_min, c_max + 1):\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            if v not in (0, 4):\n                color_cells.setdefault(v, []).append((r - r_min, c - c_min))\n    \n    first_cells = list(color_cells.values())[0]\n    rs = [r for r, c in first_cells]\n    block_size = max(rs) - min(rs) + 1\n    \n    all_colored = [(r, c) for cells in color_cells.values() for r, c in cells]\n    origin_r = min(r for r, c in all_colored)\n    origin_c = min(c for r, c in all_colored)\n    \n    template_cells = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if (r < r_min or r > r_max or c < c_min or c > c_max) and grid[r][c] != 0:\n                template_cells.append((r, c, grid[r][c]))\n    \n    t_rmin = min(r for r, c, v in template_cells)\n    t_cmin = min(c for r, c, v in template_cells)\n    \n    output = [[0] * rect_w for _ in range(rect_h)]\n    for r, c in fours:\n        output[r - r_min][c - c_min] = 4\n    \n    for r, c, color in template_cells:\n        tr, tc = r - t_rmin, c - t_cmin\n        for dr in range(block_size):\n            for dc in range(block_size):\n                out_r = origin_r + tr * block_size + dr\n                out_c = origin_c + tc * block_size + dc\n                if 0 <= out_r < rect_h and 0 <= out_c < rect_w:\n                    output[out_r][out_c] = color\n    \n    return output\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    fours = [(r, c) for r in range(rows) for c in range(cols) if grid[r][c] == 4]\n    r_min = min(r for r, c in fours)\n    r_max = max(r for r, c in fours)\n    c_min = min(c for r, c in fours)\n    c_max = max(c for r, c in fours)\n    rect_h = r_max - r_min + 1\n    rect_w = c_max - c_min + 1\n    \n    color_cells = {}\n    for r in range(r_min, r_max + 1):\n        for c in range(c_min, c_max + 1):\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            if v not in (0, 4):\n                color_cells.setdefault(v, []).append((r - r_min, c - c_min))\n    \n    first_cells = list(color_cells.values())[0]\n    rs = [r for r, c in first_cells]\n    block_size = max(rs) - min(rs) + 1\n    \n    all_colored = [(r, c) for cells in color_cells.values() for r, c in cells]\n    origin_r = min(r for r, c in all_colored)\n    origin_c = min(c for r, c in all_colored)\n    \n    template_cells = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if (r < r_min or r > r_max or c < c_min or c > c_max) and grid[r][c] != 0:\n                template_cells.append((r, c, grid[r][c]))\n    \n    t_rmin = min(r for r, c, v in template_cells)\n    t_cmin = min(c for r, c, v in template_cells)\n    \n    output = [[0] * rect_w for _ in range(rect_h)]\n    for r, c in fours:\n        output[r - r_min][c - c_min] = 4\n    \n    for r, c, color in template_cells:\n        tr, tc = r - t_rmin, c - t_cmin\n        for dr in range(block_size):\n            for dc in range(block_size):\n                out_r = origin_r + tr * block_size + dr\n                out_c = origin_c + tc * block_size + dc\n                if 0 <= out_r < rect_h and 0 <= out_c < rect_w:\n                    output[out_r][out_c] = color\n    \n    return output",
